before:
Complete local Java example; the app itself does not execute it:
```java
public class Main {
    static void change(int[] values) { values[0] = 9; }
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int[] scores = {3};
        change(scores);
        System.out.println(scores[0]);
    }
}

```

after:
void means change returns no value. Its job here is to change an array item.

```java
public class Main {
    static void change(int[] values) { values[0] = 9; }
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int[] scores = {3};
        change(scores);
        System.out.println(scores[0]);
    }
}

```
